WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.240
- Hello, my name is
Pamela Apkarian-Russell

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.840
and I am the Halloween Queen,

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.550
which is my registered trademark,

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.830
and this is Castle Halloween Museum.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.610
Welcome to Castle Halloween Museum!

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.458
Ooh, lightning!

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.780
This fireplace and mantle came
from a miniature golf course

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.383
in Windsor Locks, Connecticut.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:37.040
We have approximately 35,000
items here at the museum.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.950
48 years of collecting.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.810
Whether its folk art, pottery, paintings,

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.770
spiritualism, the Salem Witch Trials.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.463
What's a witch without her hat?

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.158
This is the Costume Room.

00:00:52.158 --> 00:00:55.050
There are over a thousand
costumes in this room.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.240
They were not flame-proof

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.060
and don't forget these people
were using live candles

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.060
at this time.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.070
Over here we cover over
a hundred years of games.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.090
But of course, you have the Ouija Board.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.070
If you're a good person,
you bring good things out.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.050
If you're a bad person, you're
gonna bring bad things out.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.770
It's you that brings the things to you.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:14.760
Memento Mori was for remembering the dead.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:16.980
They're interesting because
they're made of human hair.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:19.870
It was like having that
person there with you.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:21.380
These are the Earth Spirits.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.380
I would love to have one
of these guys come alive

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.890
in my yard and just come in here

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.920
and just be part of my life.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.050
It was junk, as far as
people were concerned.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.530
That's how I got my moniker,
the Halloween Queen.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.170
We were set up in a very posh antique show

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:39.070
and this man took great umbrage
to my big Halloween display,

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.467
really very snobbish.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.820
"I don't want all this
Halloween Queen junk."

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.597
I remember looking at him and saying,

00:01:44.597 --> 00:01:46.940
"if you don't like it, leave."

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.920
Now, especially after my books came out

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.525
and people started seeing the value

00:01:51.525 --> 00:01:54.590
and the sophistication of the artwork

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.720
and the beauty of the artwork,

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.912
then all of a sudden it started
coming out of the woodwork.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:05.730
Halloween has nothing to
do with blood and gore.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.290
It was a way of giving.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.830
It represents the harvest

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.600
and the fact that you're gonna
make it through the winter.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.943
It's the life force being kept unbroken.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.120
Real life, it can be
very, very harsh and ugly.

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.900
Halloween, it's a healing process.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.430
It's like you have a big cauldron of water

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:26.710
and you start putting in
all these wonderful spices,

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.040
whether it's the voodoo
flags, the Day of the Dead,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:33.790
the Easter Witches from
Sweden, the troll from Norway.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.000
It gathers things together.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.550
It is intolerant of intolerance.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.763
This is what makes our lives richer.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.354
Hubba hubba, dingle dangle,

00:02:44.354 --> 00:02:47.451
I can see from every angle.

00:02:47.451 --> 00:02:48.284
- Who said that?

00:02:48.284 --> 00:02:50.260
- It was in a magazine or a book

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:52.163
from a hundred thousand years ago.

